From: Huajin Wang <7976028+excelwang@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: report software TX drops through netdev core stats

The common TX failures update legacy netdev stats, but ndo_get_stats64
reports hardware drops and does not merge that legacy field. Use core
per-CPU drops, which dev_get_stats() merges with ndo_get_stats64. Keep
PON atomic accounting and NETDEV_TX_BUSY semantics unchanged.

Export of the retained 950 repair on the current upstream TX layout.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
index 5fe8abc..936f136 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3029,7 +3029,7 @@ static netdev_tx_t airoha_dev_xmit_common(
 	if (pon_data && unlikely(skb->len < ETH_ZLEN)) {
 		if (skb_put_padto(skb, ETH_ZLEN)) {
 			atomic64_inc(&dev->pon_stats.tx_dropped);
-			owner_netdev->stats.tx_dropped++;
+			dev_core_stats_tx_dropped_inc(owner_netdev);
 			spin_unlock_bh(&q->lock);
 			rcu_read_unlock();
 			return NETDEV_TX_OK;
@@ -3126,7 +3126,7 @@ error:
 	if (pon_data)
 		atomic64_inc(&dev->pon_stats.tx_dropped);
 	dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
-	owner_netdev->stats.tx_dropped++;
+	dev_core_stats_tx_dropped_inc(owner_netdev);
 	rcu_read_unlock();
 
 	return NETDEV_TX_OK;
